IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Northwest Territories Income Tax Act -- the individual's duties and deadlines, kept apart from nt-pit.l4 so that only
-- this module and those importing it load the date library.
--   s 11, applying federal s 150(1)(d) and (1.1)(b): filing the return; s 16(1) and s 17: paying the tax, by instalments or
--   by the balance-due day (federal s 248(1)); s 3.3(1) and (3): the NWT Child Benefit notices.
-- The federal provisions applied are read in the federal Act deposited at
-- subjects/ca/income-tax-act/registers/source-bundle/R.S.C.-1985-c.-1-5th-Supp..txt.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Duties of the individual under the Northwest Territories Income Tax Act`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the individual`
    `the Minister`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `file the return of income`
    `pay the March instalment`
    `pay the June instalment`
    `pay the September instalment`
    `pay the December instalment`
    `pay the remainder of the tax`
    `notify the Minister that I have ceased to be an eligible individual`

§§ `Dates`

-- Time in the regulative rules is counted in days from 1 January of the taxation year.
GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER, `day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days into` `tax year` `day` MEANS `day` MINUS (Date 1 1 `tax year`)

-- s 11(a) applies federal s 150 "for the purposes of this Act". Federal s 150(1)(d): an individual files "on or before
-- (i) the following April 30", or "(ii) the following June 15" where the individual "carried on a business in the year"
-- (other than primarily tax shelter investments) or is the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner of such an individual.
-- The rules for a deceased individual (s 150(1)(b), (d)(iii)) are not encoded.
GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `I or my cohabiting spouse carried on a business in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the filing due date` `tax year` `I or my cohabiting spouse carried on a business in the year` MEANS
    IF `I or my cohabiting spouse carried on a business in the year`
    THEN Date 15 6 (`tax year` PLUS 1)
    ELSE Date 30 4 (`tax year` PLUS 1)

-- Federal s 248(1) "balance-due day", "(c) in any other case where the taxpayer is an individual, April 30 in the
-- following taxation year" (an individual who died after October is not encoded).
GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the balance-due day` `tax year` MEANS Date 30 4 (`tax year` PLUS 1)

§§ `s 11 and federal s 150 -- must I file`

-- Federal s 150(1.1)(b): s 150(1) does not apply to an individual "unless (i) tax is payable under this Part by the
-- individual for the year, (ii) where the individual is resident in Canada at any time in the year, the individual has a
-- taxable capital gain or disposes of capital property in the year, ... or (iv) at the end of the year the individual's
-- HBP balance or LLP balance ... is a positive amount." Read for this Act: tax payable under the territorial Act.
-- (s 150(1)(e), a return demanded by the Minister's notice, is a further case, asked as a fact.)
GIVEN `tax is payable by me under the Act for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I had a taxable capital gain or disposed of capital property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have a positive HBP or LLP balance at the end of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister demanded a return by notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I must file a return under s 11 and federal s 150` IF
        `tax is payable by me under the Act for the year`
    OR  `I had a taxable capital gain or disposed of capital property`
    OR  `I have a positive HBP or LLP balance at the end of the year`
    OR  `the Minister demanded a return by notice`

GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `I or my cohabiting spouse carried on a business in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I must file` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to file` `tax year` `I or my cohabiting spouse carried on a business in the year` `I must file` MEANS
    IF `I must file`
    THEN PARTY `the individual`
         MUST  `file the return of income`
         WITHIN `days into` `tax year` (`the filing due date` `tax year` `I or my cohabiting spouse carried on a business in the year`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "return not filed by the date in federal s 150(1)(d), applied by s 11"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `ss 16 and 17 -- paying the tax`

-- s 16(1): every individual (other than a farmer or fisher under s 15, or one whose tax is withheld under federal s 153(2))
-- "shall pay ... (a) on or before March 15, June 15, September 15 and December 15 in the year, an amount equal to
-- one-quarter of (i) the amount estimated ... to be the tax payable ... for the year, or (ii) the tax payable ... for the
-- immediately preceding taxation year; and (b) on or before the individual's balance-due day for the year, the remainder".
-- s 17: "Where no federal instalments are required by virtue of section 156.1 of the federal Act", s 16 does not apply and
-- the individual pays the estimated tax "on or before the individual's balance-due day". Whether federal instalments are
-- required (federal s 156.1, net tax owing over the instalment threshold) is asked as a fact.
GIVEN `the instalment base` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each quarterly instalment under s 16(1)(a)` `the instalment base` MEANS `the instalment base` DIVIDED BY 4

GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `federal instalments are required of me under s 156.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to pay the tax` `tax year` `federal instalments are required of me under s 156.1` MEANS
    IF `federal instalments are required of me under s 156.1`
    THEN     (PARTY `the individual`
              MUST  `pay the March instalment`
              WITHIN `days into` `tax year` (Date 15 3 `tax year`)
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "March 15 instalment not paid (s 16(1)(a))")
         RAND
             (PARTY `the individual`
              MUST  `pay the June instalment`
              WITHIN `days into` `tax year` (Date 15 6 `tax year`)
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "June 15 instalment not paid (s 16(1)(a))")
         RAND
             (PARTY `the individual`
              MUST  `pay the September instalment`
              WITHIN `days into` `tax year` (Date 15 9 `tax year`)
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "September 15 instalment not paid (s 16(1)(a))")
         RAND
             (PARTY `the individual`
              MUST  `pay the December instalment`
              WITHIN `days into` `tax year` (Date 15 12 `tax year`)
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "December 15 instalment not paid (s 16(1)(a))")
         RAND
             (PARTY `the individual`
              MUST  `pay the remainder of the tax`
              WITHIN `days into` `tax year` (`the balance-due day` `tax year`)
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "remainder not paid by the balance-due day (s 16(1)(b))")
    ELSE PARTY `the individual`
         MUST  `pay the remainder of the tax`
         WITHIN `days into` `tax year` (`the balance-due day` `tax year`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "tax not paid by the balance-due day (s 17)"

§§ `s 3.3 -- the NWT Child Benefit notices`

-- s 3.3(1): a person is an eligible individual for a month "only if the person has, no later than 11 months after the
-- end of the month, filed with the Minister a notice in prescribed form" (s 3.3(2): the Minister may extend the time).
-- The last day: the last day of the eleventh month after the month.
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to file the s 3.3(1) notice for a month` `month` `year` MEANS
    (Date 1 m2 y2) MINUS 1
    WHERE
        k  MEANS (`month` MINUS 1) PLUS 12
        m2 MEANS (k MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        y2 MEANS `year` PLUS FLOOR (k DIVIDED BY 12)

-- s 3.3(3): "Where during a particular month a person ceases to be an eligible individual in respect of a particular
-- qualified dependant (otherwise than because of the qualified dependant attaining the age of 18 years), the person shall
-- notify the Minister of that fact before the end of the first month following the particular month."
GIVEN `the day I ceased to be eligible` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to notify under s 3.3(3)` `the day I ceased to be eligible` MEANS
    (Date 1 m2 y2) MINUS 1
    WHERE
        k  MEANS (DATE_MONTH `the day I ceased to be eligible` MINUS 1) PLUS 2
        m2 MEANS (k MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        y2 MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day I ceased to be eligible` PLUS FLOOR (k DIVIDED BY 12)

-- Time counted in days from the day the person ceased to be eligible.
GIVEN `the day I ceased to be eligible` IS A DATE
      `because the child turned 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to notify that I ceased to be eligible` `the day I ceased to be eligible` `because the child turned 18` MEANS
    IF `because the child turned 18`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the individual`
         MUST  `notify the Minister that I have ceased to be an eligible individual`
         WITHIN (`the last day to notify under s 3.3(3)` `the day I ceased to be eligible`) MINUS `the day I ceased to be eligible`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "the Minister was not told before the end of the month after the person ceased to be an eligible individual (s 3.3(3))"
